  {
   "id": "cl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 698,
   "width": 678,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100062,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700434,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Routing tiles: graph data, and deliberately NOT a graph database",
   "originalText": "Routing tiles: graph data, and deliberately NOT a graph database",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "rt",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 736,
   "width": 820,
   "height": 150,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100063,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700441,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "rt_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "rt_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 758,
   "width": 804,
   "height": 105,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100064,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700448,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "routing_tile:  (version, geohash, detail_level)  ->  bytes\n\n# inside the blob, a compact binary encoding:\n#   nodes[]:    intersection id, lat, lng\n#   edges[]:    from_node, to_node, length_m, road_class, speed_limit,\n#               turn_restrictions, segment_id  <- the join key to traffic\n#   boundary[]: neighbouring tile refs + the nodes where roads cross out",
   "originalText": "routing_tile:  (version, geohash, detail_level)  ->  bytes\n\n# inside the blob, a compact binary encoding:\n#   nodes[]:    intersection id, lat, lng\n#   edges[]:    from_node, to_node, length_m, road_class, speed_limit,\n#               turn_restrictions, segment_id  <- the join key to traffic\n#   boundary[]: neighbouring tile refs + the nodes where roads cross out",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "rt",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 736,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 90,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100065,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700455,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Because there is no graph QUERY to run. The navigation service does not ask 'find\nme a path' of the store - it asks 'give me tile 9q8yy at level 3' and runs its\nown A* in memory. A graph database's value is SERVER-SIDE TRAVERSAL, and here\ntraversal must happen in the application because it needs custom heuristics,\nlevel transitions and per-request user filters. You would be paying for a\ntraversal engine you cannot use.",
   "originalText": "Because there is no graph QUERY to run. The navigation service does not ask 'find\nme a path' of the store - it asks 'give me tile 9q8yy at level 3' and runs its\nown A* in memory. A graph database's value is SERVER-SIDE TRAVERSAL, and here\ntraversal must happen in the application because it needs custom heuristics,\nlevel transitions and per-request user filters. You would be paying for a\ntraversal engine you cannot use.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 848,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100066,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700462,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And the blob is a compact BINARY format, not JSON: edges are fixed-width records\nso the in-memory representation is close to the on-disk one - no parse step, and\nadjacency can be an array index rather than a pointer chase. That matters because\nthe search is bounded by MEMORY LATENCY rather than by graph size, and\ncache-friendly layout is the direct lever on it.",
   "originalText": "And the blob is a compact BINARY format, not JSON: edges are fixed-width records\nso the in-memory representation is close to the on-disk one - no parse step, and\nadjacency can be an array index rather than a pointer chase. That matters because\nthe search is bounded by MEMORY LATENCY rather than by graph size, and\ncache-friendly layout is the direct lever on it.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 932,
   "width": 914,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100067,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700469,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "segment_id is the join key that makes the ETA separation work: the tile carries STATIC properties only, and live\ntravel time is looked up by segment_id from the traffic store. That is what lets weights change every few seconds\nwhile tiles stay immutable - a separation of change rates, expressed as a foreign key.",
   "originalText": "segment_id is the join key that makes the ETA separation work: the tile carries STATIC properties only, and live\ntravel time is looked up by segment_id from the traffic store. That is what lets weights change every few seconds\nwhile tiles stay immutable - a separation of change rates, expressed as a foreign key.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d4",
