   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100079,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700553,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "CREATE TABLE segment_speed_history (\n    segment_id   bigint,\n    day_of_week  smallint,   -- 0-6\n    time_bucket  smallint,   -- 15-minute bucket, 0-95\n    p50_speed    float,\n    p85_speed    float,\n    sample_count int,\n    PRIMARY KEY (segment_id, day_of_week, time_bucket)\n);",
   "originalText": "CREATE TABLE segment_speed_history (\n    segment_id   bigint,\n    day_of_week  smallint,   -- 0-6\n    time_bucket  smallint,   -- 15-minute bucket, 0-95\n    p50_speed    float,\n    p85_speed    float,\n    sample_count int,\n    PRIMARY KEY (segment_id, day_of_week, time_bucket)\n);",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "agg",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 1436,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100080,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700560,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "100M segments x 7 days x 96 buckets is ~67 billion rows at ~30 bytes = about 2 TB\nTOTAL, not per day. THIS IS THE ACTUAL PRODUCT OF THE LOCATION PIPELINE, and\neverything upstream is scaffolding.",
   "originalText": "100M segments x 7 days x 96 buckets is ~67 billion rows at ~30 bytes = about 2 TB\nTOTAL, not per day. THIS IS THE ACTUAL PRODUCT OF THE LOCATION PIPELINE, and\neverything upstream is scaffolding.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1508,
   "width": 1003,
   "height": 81,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100081,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700567,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why Cassandra: 694,000 appends/sec with essentially no interactive reads - the most write-skewed workload in the system. LSM\nstorage makes every write a sequential memtable append, where a relational store would spend its life on random page updates\nand index maintenance for rows nobody queries. And (user_id, bucket) rather than user_id alone because an active user\ncontributes ~17,000 samples/day and millions per year: a Cassandra partition is the unit of storage AND of repair, so\nunbounded growth is an operational problem long before it is a storage one.",
   "originalText": "Why Cassandra: 694,000 appends/sec with essentially no interactive reads - the most write-skewed workload in the system. LSM\nstorage makes every write a sequential memtable append, where a relational store would spend its life on random page updates\nand index maintenance for rows nobody queries. And (user_id, bucket) rather than user_id alone because an active user\ncontributes ~17,000 samples/day and millions per year: a Cassandra partition is the unit of storage AND of repair, so\nunbounded growth is an operational problem long before it is a storage one.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1620,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100082,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700574,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "float is CORRECT here, unlike money. A float32 resolves latitude to ~1 metre, well below consumer GPS accuracy (3-10 m in the\nopen, far worse among buildings) - the MEASUREMENT error dwarfs the representation error, so precision loss is unobservable.\nMoney has no measurement error, which is what makes representation error the only error there is.",
   "originalText": "float is CORRECT here, unlike money. A float32 resolves latitude to ~1 metre, well below consumer GPS accuracy (3-10 m in the\nopen, far worse among buildings) - the MEASUREMENT error dwarfs the representation error, so precision loss is unobservable.\nMoney has no measurement error, which is what makes representation error the only error there is.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en4",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1700,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 113,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100083,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700581,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And default_time_to_live = 7776000 is a DESIGN POSITION, not a default. What the product actually needs is aggregate speed per\nsegment per time-of-day - a tiny derived table - so the raw traces expire and the aggregates persist. TWCS makes that expiry\ndrop whole SSTables rather than rewriting them: delete a file, not a row. Two reasons the aggregate is essential rather than\nnice-to-have: a route requested for 8am TOMORROW has no live traffic to consult, and it is the fallback whenever a live\nsegment's TTL has expired - the common case for minor roads with few sampled vehicles. p85_speed sits alongside p50 because\nfor an ETA people rely on, the pessimistic percentile is often the more useful number: an estimate that is right half the time\nis worse than one that is conservative.",
   "originalText": "And default_time_to_live = 7776000 is a DESIGN POSITION, not a default. What the product actually needs is aggregate speed per\nsegment per time-of-day - a tiny derived table - so the raw traces expire and the aggregates persist. TWCS makes that expiry\ndrop whole SSTables rather than rewriting them: delete a file, not a row. Two reasons the aggregate is essential rather than\nnice-to-have: a route requested for 8am TOMORROW has no live traffic to consult, and it is the fallback whenever a live\nsegment's TTL has expired - the common case for minor roads with few sampled vehicles. p85_speed sits alongside p50 because\nfor an ETA people rely on, the pessimistic percentile is often the more useful number: an estimate that is right half the time\nis worse than one that is conservative.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
