   "versionNonce": 700651,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Nothing in this system requires strong consistency anywhere - and that is the deep reason multi-region is easy",
   "originalText": "Nothing in this system requires strong consistency anywhere - and that is the deep reason multi-region is easy",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2272,
   "width": 1027,
   "height": 292,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100094,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700658,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "map tiles            immutable per version; eventually consistent across edges   a client is always on exactly ONE coherent\n                                                                                version, so there is no torn state. Version lag\n                                                                                just means some clients are on v41 and some on\n                                                                                v42 - both correct.\nrouting tiles        immutable per version                                      a route is computed entirely within one\n                                                                                version, so it cannot mix graphs\nlive traffic speeds  eventual, seconds; last-write-wins                         an aggregate over a time window, so two\n                                                                                aggregators produce the same value - which is\n                                                                                why no leader election is needed\nlocation history     eventual, at-least-once                                    a duplicate row with the same key is an\n                                                                                idempotent overwrite, so DUPLICATION IS\n                                                                                HARMLESS BY CONSTRUCTION and exactly-once\n                                                                                would be wasted effort\ntraffic aggregates   eventual, batch                                            a slightly stale historical average is\n                                                                                indistinguishable from a current one\nroute responses      a READ-ONLY SNAPSHOT                                       weights are read once at the start, so the\n                                                                                route is internally consistent even if the\n                                                                                world moved during computation",
   "originalText": "map tiles            immutable per version; eventually consistent across edges   a client is always on exactly ONE coherent\n                                                                                version, so there is no torn state. Version lag\n                                                                                just means some clients are on v41 and some on\n                                                                                v42 - both correct.\nrouting tiles        immutable per version                                      a route is computed entirely within one\n                                                                                version, so it cannot mix graphs\nlive traffic speeds  eventual, seconds; last-write-wins                         an aggregate over a time window, so two\n                                                                                aggregators produce the same value - which is\n                                                                                why no leader election is needed\nlocation history     eventual, at-least-once                                    a duplicate row with the same key is an\n                                                                                idempotent overwrite, so DUPLICATION IS\n                                                                                HARMLESS BY CONSTRUCTION and exactly-once\n                                                                                would be wasted effort\ntraffic aggregates   eventual, batch                                            a slightly stale historical average is\n                                                                                indistinguishable from a current one\nroute responses      a READ-ONLY SNAPSHOT                                       weights are read once at the start, so the\n                                                                                route is internally consistent even if the\n                                                                                world moved during computation",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2604,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100095,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700665,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Every datum is either IMMUTABLE (tiles), STATISTICAL (traffic) or SELF-CORRECTING (positions). There is no global invariant to\nprotect - which is exactly why multi-region is easy here and the hardest unsolved problem in the digital wallet. And the\ntraffic aggregate has a genuinely pleasant scaling property: its row count is segments x days x buckets, so it does not grow\nwith usage at all.",
   "originalText": "Every datum is either IMMUTABLE (tiles), STATISTICAL (traffic) or SELF-CORRECTING (positions). There is no global invariant to\nprotect - which is exactly why multi-region is easy here and the hardest unsolved problem in the digital wallet. And the\ntraffic aggregate has a genuinely pleasant scaling property: its row count is segments x days x buckets, so it does not grow\nwith usage at all.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d8",
